      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Enantiopure S-H2L (from NaBH4 reduction of the Schiff base of aromatic aldehyde and asparagine) was mixed with Ni(ClO4)2·6H2O and Dy(NO3)3·6H2O in water at 80 °C for 1 h to generate S-[DyNiL2]+ building units (HRESI-MS). Under basic conditions the deprotonated carboxylates polymerize the units, and oxalate-assisted crystallization yields the P double helix [Dy5Ni5(S-L)10(C2O4)(H2O)10](NO3)(ClO4)2·16H2O. Numerical reagent amounts are not given in the main-text procedure.",
